# Handbook first (non-negotiable)

`docs/handbook/` is the project source of truth. **[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)** aligns with it.

## Before editing code

On **substantive** work (features, refactors, auth/OAuth, crates/Prisma, App Router handlers, CSS/layout, tests for new behavior, CI/env):

1. **Read** `docs/handbook/non-negotiables.md` (digest + context efficiency).
2. **Route** via `docs/handbook/llms.md` → read **only matching chapters** before the first code change (each chapter **once** per task; Grep/Glob before opening large files).
3. **Reuse documented patterns** — extend existing hooks/components; do not reimplement parallel logic.

**Substantive = read handbook first.** Narrow mechanical fixes (obvious typos, single-line fixes with unchanged behavior) may skip a full pass.

## During implementation

- **Testing non-negotiables** — TDD, **factories**, flat hook **`describe`**, **API mocks in POs** (not in **`.spec.tsx`**). See [non-negotiables.md](docs/handbook/non-negotiables.md) and [testing.md](docs/handbook/testing.md).
- **Stacked branches (`st`)** — **`st`** / gh-stack on **`staging`**. See [non-negotiables.md](docs/handbook/non-negotiables.md) and [platform.md](docs/handbook/platform.md).
- **Conventions** — follow routed chapters ([conventions.md](docs/handbook/conventions.md), [react.md](docs/handbook/react.md), [css.md](docs/handbook/css.md), [testing.md](docs/handbook/testing.md)).
- **UI state defaults** — check whether an existing hook already owns them (e.g. `useCrateDrawer`: `userToggled ?? isDesktop`; login uses `resetDrawer()`, not duplicate breakpoint checks).
- **Optional props** — `classNames()` / `definedProps()` ([react.md](docs/handbook/react.md)).
- **CSS** — mobile-first `(width >= …)`; nest under blocks ([css.md](docs/handbook/css.md)).
- **Auth/session** — verified OAuth on data routes; patterns in [discogs.md](docs/handbook/discogs.md) + [patterns.md](docs/handbook/patterns.md).

## Before finishing

- **Post-work handbook sync (same turn as the last code change):** If **`src/`**, **`.jest/`**, **`jest.config.ts`**, **`e2e/`**, **`playwright.config.ts`**, **`next.config.ts`**, or test conventions changed, update the matching **`docs/handbook/*.md`** chapter(s) **before** your final reply — route via **`llms.md`**, cite section headings when confirming no doc update was needed. Cursor **`stop`** hook [`session-stop-checks.sh`](../../.cursor/hooks/session-stop-checks.sh) and CI **`pnpm handbook:check`** ([`handbook-sync-check.sh`](../../scripts/handbook-sync-check.sh), [`spec-pair-check.sh`](../../scripts/spec-pair-check.sh)) enforce handbook sync and playback/util/hook spec pairing.
- If behavior, files, or conventions changed → **update the matching `docs/handbook/*.md` chapter** in the same PR (or immediate follow-up). Do not leave the handbook stale.
- If **user-facing features, routes, setup, or tech stack** listed in the root **README** changed → update **`README.md`** in the same change (hooks nudge this for pages, login features, mise/tool-versions, `package.json`, platform setup).
- Run relevant checks from the chapter (e.g. `pnpm lint:css`, targeted tests).

## If unsure

Search the handbook for the feature area; read that chapter. Do not guess project conventions from chat memory alone.
